rmer parallelism), though the real question is whether those heads are actually being used or just declared. Then there's the 7th layer enforcement, the \"paint wall\" metaphor, involving a pre-activation identity gate that verifies an agent card before any compute happens.\n\nThis coating is forced, not something you can skip past as a checkpoint - it's immutable from the agent's side, read-only from below and write-only from above, with head utilization checked passively and reports flowing upward into remediation. The whole thing forms a self-healing loop of reporting, remediation, documentation, and learning, and documentation itself is non-negotiable for progress and credibility. Time to move: scale the BFT swarm test to real numbers (65K+ nodes, pushing toward millions), document the SQLite bottleneck, codify the paint wall mechanism, put the 26B Gemma model to real work, and write it all down. No more stalling.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"bash ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh maxx \\\"Acknowledged. Correcting the Byzantine swarm to real scale. Updating the seventh layer paint wall gate. Documenting everything. Moving.\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Speaking via Maxx\"","toolSummary":"\"Audio dispatch\""}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"grep -rn \\\"1024\\\\|1,024\\\\|num_nodes.*1024\\\\|TOTAL_NODES.*1024\\\\|n_nodes.*1024\\\" --include=\\\"*.py\\\" --include=\\\"*.zig\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" --include=\\\"*.rs\\\" ops/ AI_Core/ memory/ docs/ 2>/dev/null | head -30\"","Cwd":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Finding stale 1024 placeholder references\"","toolSummary":"\"Find 1024 placeholder refs\""}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"grep -rn \\\"148\\\\|num_nodes\\\\|total_nodes\\\\|TOTAL_NODES\\\\|n_