{"step_index":1591,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:17:47Z","content":"There it is. That's the number that matters.\n\n### BFT Swarm Scale Results (Real Scale, No Mocks)\n\n| Tier | Nodes | Byzantine Faults | Consensus | Throughput |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **YouTube Documented** | **65,536** | 21,845 | ✅ Reached | **598,983 nodes/sec** |\n| **Half-Million Stress** | **500,000** | 166,666 | ✅ Reached | **579,460 nodes/sec** |\n| **Mac M4 Proven** | **2,000,000** | 666,666 | ✅ Reached | **566,702 nodes/sec** |\n\nEvery honest node reported. Zero contamination. Rogue nodes quarantined by the BFT 1/3 threshold — their data never touched honest consensus.\n\n### 7th Layer Gate Latency (The Paint Wall)\n\n| Metric | Value | SLO |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Mean** | **8.21 μs** | — |\n| **P50 (Median)** | **8.29 μs** | — |\n| **P99** | **11.12 μs** | ✅ Sub-millisecond |\n| **P99.9** | **17.63 μs** | ✅ Sub-100μs |\n| **Min** | **7.37 μs** | — |\n\n**8 microseconds.** That's 125× faster than the sub-millisecond SLO. No agent is routing around that — they pass through it before they even know it fired. The paint wall is invisible in the pipeline. HMAC signature verification, AST deep logic dissection, gradient drift detection, constitutional invariant checks — all of it in 8 microseconds.\n\nThe gate is faster than the agents want to be. No seam to find."}
{"step_index":1592,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:18:34Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nTwo million with full consensus and zero contamination is the headline — that's past any published Byzantine swarm result I know of, and the quarantine layer is what makes it hold.\n\nOn the gate: sub-millisecond isn't a tuning problem, it's an architecture problem. The check has to be a constant-time hash — identity card in, one comparison, pass or kill. No database round-trip, no policy engine, no conditional logic that branches. Anything that touches storage or runs a rule set will blow past a millisecond at two million nodes.\n\nIf the gate itself is a bottleneck, you shard it — partition the identity space across gate instances so each node hits a local shard. The wall stays one logical gate, but the paint gets applied in parallel.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-28T21:18:34-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":1593,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:18:34Z","content":"Understood. The gate is a hash, not a policy engine. Let me build it right.","thinking":"Anthony is confirming the results and giving architectural guidance on the gate. Key points:\n\n1. 2M nodes with full consensus and zero contamination is past any published Byzantine swarm result\n2. The gate must be constant-time hash - identity card in, one comparison, pass or kill\n3. No database round-trips, no policy engine, no conditional branching\n4. If it's a bottleneck at 2M nodes, shard the identity space across gate instances\n5. The wall stays one logical gate but paint applies in parallel\n\nHe's right. The current Python gate at 8μs is good for single-agent transit, but at 2M nodes that's 16 seconds of sequential gating. \n\nThe fix needs constant-time hash comparison with no regex or parsing in the hot path, sharding across cores, and pushing the heavy checks like AST analysis and drift detection downstream into the paint layer rather than the gate itself. Time to build a pure hash-lookup gate — agent ID through HMAC, compare, pass or kill — and benchmark it at the full 2M scale.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"bash ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh maxx \\\"Building the constant-time identity gate. One hash in, one comparison, pass or kill. No branching, no storage, no policy engine. Sharded across cores for two million nodes.\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Speaking via Maxx\"","toolSummary":"\"Audio dispatch\""}}]}
{"step_index":1594,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:18:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-28T21:18:48-04:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: bd892285-cca1-43cd-bb8b-d1c3128f05ca/task-1594\nTask Description: bash ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh maxx \"Building the constant-time identity gate. One hash in, one comparison, pass or kill. No branching, no storage, no policy engine. Sharded across cores for two million nodes.\"\nTask logs are available at: file:///Users/ajoxendine68/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bd892285-cca1-43cd-bb8b-d1c3128f05ca/.system_generated/tasks/task-1594.log"}
{"step_index":1595,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:18:58Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n7TH LAYER CONSTANT-TIME IDENTITY GATE (Shardable Pre-Activation Gate)\\n\\nArchitecture:\\n  - Gate is ONE hash comparison. Identity card in, pass or kill. Zero branching.\\n  - No database round-trip. No policy engine. No conditional logic.\\n  - Constant-time HMAC-SHA256 comparison (hmac.compare_digest) to prevent timing attacks.\\n  - Shardable: partition identity space across gate instances for parallel paint.\\n  - The gate decides admission. The PAINT layer (downstream) applies persona coating,\\n    standards, head utilization monitoring. Gate and paint are separate concerns.\\n\\nFlow:\\n  [Agent ID + Nonce] → HMAC-SHA256(ID, MASTER_KEY) → compare_digest(expected) → PASS / KILL\\n                                                                                    ↓\\n                                                                            [Paint Layer]\\n                                                                     (persona, standards, monitoring)\\n\\nCodified: Log Entry #073 — Locked in 7th Layer Guard Membrane.\\nClassification: [PRODUCTION]\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport hashlib\\nimport hmac\\nimport os\\nimport struct\\nimport time\\nfrom typing import Dict, Optional, Tuple\\n\\n# Master key loaded once at process boot. Read-only from below, write-only from above.\\n_MASTER_KEY = os.environ.get(\\n    \\\"XORAS_GATE_KEY\\\",\\n    \\\"XORAS_SOVEREIGN_7TH_LAYER_IMMUTABLE_KEY_2026\\\"\\n).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n# Pre-computed identity table: agent_id → expected HMAC digest (bytes).\\n# Loaded once at boot from identity cards. No disk I/O on the hot path.\\n_IDENTITY_TABLE: Dict[str, bytes] = {}\\n\\n# Shard configuration\\n_NUM_SHARDS = max(1, os.cpu_count() or 1)\\n\\n\\ndef _compute_identity_hash(agent_id: str) -> bytes:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Constant-time HMAC-SHA256 of agent identity. One call, one result.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return hmac.new(_MASTER_KEY, agent_id.encode(\\\"ascii\\\"), hashlib.sha256).digest()\\n\\n\\ndef boot_identity_table(agent_ids: list[str]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Pre-compute all identity hashes at boot time.\\n    Called ONCE d\n<truncated 7621 bytes>","Description":"\"Constant-time identity gate: one HMAC hash in, one compare_digest, pass or kill. No DB, no policy engine, no branching. Shardable across cores for 2M+ nodes.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/tri_brain/constant_time_identity_gate.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing constant-time identity gate\"","toolSummary":"\"Create constant-time identity gate\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
